 "name": "City Flat",
 "notes": "A 48 by 32 metre city block: two flats either side of a shared stairwell hall, and a flat roof over the lot with washing lines (floor 3 m). The west flat has the living room, kitchen, bathroom and bedroom; the east flat mirrors it with the lounge, diner, bathroom and kids' room. Stairs climb to the roof from the hall and from the corner of each living room, so the roof is a second way between the flats. X is east, Z is north, in metres; yaw is degrees clockwise from north; furniture 'y' is height above the room floor. Rooms marked outdoor have no ceiling and a garden or paved floor.",
